document.write('Joel Soroka Gallery presents “Before the Dawn”, a solo show of the artist Franco Donaggio Opening : 15th December 2010, 19:00, 16th December 2010 - 15th April 2011 JOEL SOROKA GALLERY 400 East Hyman Avenue, Aspen, CO 81611 The Joel Soroka Gallery in Aspen dedicates the winter exhibition to wellknown artist Franco Donaggio. From 15 December 2010 to 15 April 2011 it will be possible to admire the works of his new job “Before the dawn”. Thanks to his most personal poetics, the artist moves with deep insight into an imaginary world bending photography to the purposes of his surreal-like research, and creating images which are very powerful and expressive. In admiring Franco Donaggio’s works in an imposing large-sized black and white, you feel you are more a traveller than an observer, a traveller following a new path made of intense and odd sensations rising from the artist’s remote interior places which are eventually made visible. Places that are built with intuitions, emotions, conjectures. Places that are difficult to express through photography, but Donaggio succeeded in making them manifest - somewhat irrepressible - in his work. Donaggio creates a landscape that seems to spring from imagination or desire, where everything assumes a fascinating greatness. Here nothing looks real, even if we feel it is. Franco Donaggio Chioggia (VE), Italy 1958 Donaggio moves to Milan in 1979 and works in the field of advertising communication as photographer and graphic designer. Several of his works were hosted in galleries and museums in Europe and the United States, while others are part of public and private photographic collections. He was the recipient of the Italian “Kodak Gold Award” for the creative portrait and of the “Gran Prix Award” for still life photography. He has been represented since 1996 in the States and France for the sale of his works in the collection market. Franco Donaggio at ionone www.donaggioart.it JOEL SOROKA GALLERY');
